@startuml correction-component-map
' Component + data-flow map for hierarchical spelling/grammar correction.
' Four crates are wired into the pipeline (libgrammstein, libdictenstein,
' liblevenshtein, lling-llang); duallity is the ecosystem's Levenshtein->WFST
' adapter, shown detached because libgrammstein does not depend on it. One colour
' per crate; arrows show the acyclic dependency DAG and the artifacts each crate
' contributes to a correction.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/correction-component-map.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 1 in docs/integration/lling-llang/hierarchical-correction.md §2.
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
title Component & data-flow map — who provides each dimension

rectangle "**libdictenstein**\nDictionary / DictionaryNode traits\nPersistentVocabARTrie (lock-free, UTF-8)" as dict #37474F
rectangle "**liblevenshtein**\nLevenshtein automaton (Transducer)\n+ Zompist phonetics" as lev #1565C0
rectangle "**lling-llang**\nWFST framework: Lattice, semirings,\nCorrectionLayer, compose, viterbi / nbest" as llang #6A1B9A
rectangle "**libgrammstein**\nGoogle-Books LM factory:\nModified Kneser-Ney n-gram + subword embeddings" as gram #2E7D32
rectangle "**duallity**  (ecosystem — NOT a libgrammstein dep)\nLevenshteinWfst: wraps the liblevenshtein\nautomaton as an lling-llang FST for compose" as dual #90A4AE

rectangle "vocabulary\n(term ↔ u64)" as vocab #455A64
rectangle "MKN n-gram + embeddings" as lm #455A64
rectangle "LevenshteinCorrectionLayer  (libgrammstein)\n(Transducer over the vocab)" as spell #1565C0
rectangle "LanguageModelLayer\n(GrammsteinLanguageModel)" as lmlayer #2E7D32

' dependency DAG (acyclic): who depends on whom
lev --> dict : Dictionary trait
llang ..> lev : opt (levenshtein)
llang ..> dict : opt (lattice)
gram --> dict
gram --> lev
gram ..> llang : opt (integration)
dual .[#90A4AE,dashed].> lev : ecosystem
dual .[#90A4AE,dashed].> llang : ecosystem

' data flow into a correction
gram --> vocab
gram --> lm
vocab --> spell : traversed in place\n(persistent trie)
lev --> spell : automaton
lm --> lmlayer : score_continuation()
spell --> llang : DIM 1 (orthographic)
lmlayer --> llang : DIM 4+5 (contextual+semantic)

legend right
  | Colour | Crate / role |
  |<#37474F> | libdictenstein — dictionary substrate |
  |<#1565C0> | liblevenshtein — edit-distance automaton |
  |<#6A1B9A> | lling-llang — WFST host |
  |<#2E7D32> | libgrammstein — LM factory |
  |<#90A4AE> | duallity — ecosystem adapter (not a libgrammstein dep) |
endlegend
@enduml
